// LEDGER item 47, adjacent-shape gate (2026-08-28): the ENUM twin of
// `attack_mono_struct_growing_selfref_no_depth_guard_hang.kry`. Same
// growing-wrapper trick (`Wrap<T>` composed at every level so the mangled
// name is never the same twice), routed through `monomorphize_enum`
// instead of `monomorphize_struct` -- the two functions are separate call
// sites and the fix must guard BOTH independently (the struct-only fix
// would leave this shape hanging).
//
// Mechanism: `EBox<T> { Nil, Cons(T, EBox<Wrap<T>>) }` -- constructing the
// base value `EBox<i64>` via the nullary `Nil` variant still forces
// `monomorphize_enum` to substitute EVERY variant's field types (including
// the recursive `Cons(T, EBox<Wrap<T>>)` payload), which recurses into
// `monomorphize_enum(ctx, "EBox", [Wrap<i64>])` for a distinct, never-cached
// mangled name -- no variant needs to be actually constructed for the
// unbounded recursion to fire.
//
// BEFORE the item 47 fix: hangs `kryos run` indefinitely with unbounded
// RSS growth (measured on the struct twin: 5.6GB -> 8.2GB in 8s), zero
// stdout, no diagnostic. AFTER the fix: `kryos run` fails fast (< 1s) with
// a clean `mono_fatal` E0113 diagnostic naming `Wrap`, depth 301.

struct Wrap<T> {
    val: T,
}

enum EBox<T> {
    Nil,
    Cons(T, EBox<Wrap<T>>),
}

fn main() {
    let e: EBox<i64> = Nil
    println("built EBox<i64>")
}
